00:29:55.990 --> 00:29:59.210
And we are back now
running in cluster SQL1.

00:29:59.210 --> 00:30:01.430
So this is like
testing how you would

00:30:01.430 --> 00:30:03.320
do like a planned failover.

00:30:03.320 --> 00:30:06.044
So now let's plan to do
like an unplanned failover.

00:30:06.044 --> 00:30:07.460
What I'm going to
do for this one,

00:30:07.460 --> 00:30:10.800
I'm just going to restart
cluster SQL1 since that's

00:30:10.800 --> 00:30:13.270
a currently active node.

00:30:13.270 --> 00:30:18.980
